# PII-gate ruling for this repository.
#
# Format:  <key><TAB><reason>
#   name entries   key = <relative path>:<matched string>   (pii-names.py)
#   shape entries  key = <exact matched string>             (pii-shape.py)
#
# The name key is COMPOUND on purpose. An entry keyed on the name alone would
# suppress that person everywhere, including in leaked prose — the hole this
# gate exists to close. This says "this name, in this file, deliberately", and
# nowhere else. An allowlist of exact facts closes behind itself.
#
# Every line needs a reason. A line with no reason is not a ruling, it is a
# silencer. Ruled 2026-08-27 at v0.3.0, by reading every finding.
#
# There are no name entries: this repository names no people.

# ── Shape findings: capitalized bigrams that are not people. The shape scanner
# flags name-shaped pairs it cannot place; each of these is a product name, an
# identifier, an anatomical term, or an example graph statement.

Claude Desktop	product name — the stdio transport's example client, in README.md and packaging metadata
Upgraded FastMCP	changelog bullet — sentence-initial verb followed by the library name
The Cypher	query language name in a server docstring
List Node Types	tool name — list_node_types, title-cased in a docstring
List Relation Types	tool name — list_relation_types, title-cased in a docstring
Raises ValueError	Python exception name in a docstring Raises: clause
Enum Tests	test class heading in test_server.py
The Entorhinal	anatomical term — "The Entorhinal-Hippocampal Gateway", an EdgeConfiguration example in HOWTO.xml
The Fear Valence Circuit GENERATES	example graph statement in HOWTO.xml — EdgeConfiguration name plus relation type
The Braak Staging Progression SUPPORTS Constitutive Relationality	example graph statement in HOWTO.xml — EmpiricalEvidence name, relation type, TheoreticalPrinciple name
The Docker	product name fragment, sentence-initial in release notes
